title: StartDay2
position: 90,-43
---
<<set $daysPassed = 62>>
<<declare $day2KeptUnderWraps = false>>
<<play_sound AlarmClock>>
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
I wake up to a loud chime on the monitor, my head <color=\#FF8888>pounding yet again</color>.
Cryosleep leaves a gap you can feel in your bones. The mission clock doesn't.
I blink at the readout until it stops swimming.
Day {$daysPassed}.
Two months have passed in the span of one sleep.
Yet, the memory of the alien encounter is still warm, too vivid to be a dream.
<<show_ui ClickToInteract>>
<<show MonitorOffDay2>>
===

title: OnClickedMonitorDay2
position: 85,114
---
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I power the monitor on, expecting the comfort of routine. The same checklist, the same empty horizon, the same report no one reads.
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
Instead, the communication panel pings, sharp and insistent. Locked onto a frequency I didn't dial in.
Three new packets sit in the buffer, tagged with an unknown sequence.
The ship's translator does what it can. It renders the signals into clipped, robotic phonemes.
It isn't a sentence. It's a pulse. A test pattern that learned three words.
<<speed 0.4>>
<<play_sound RobotTest 0.25>>
"TEST" <i>[79 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<play_sound RobotHello 0.25>>
"HELLO" <i>[41 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<play_sound RobotTalk 0.25>>
"TALK" <i>[5 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<speed 1>>
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
My fingers hover over the response key. The <color=\#FF8888>dread is already settling in</color>.
The encounter wasn't a fever dream...
<<speed 0.4>>
<<play_sound RobotTest 0.25>>
"TEST" <i>[79 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<play_sound RobotHello 0.25>>
"HELLO" <i>[41 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<play_sound RobotTalk 0.25>>
"TALK" <i>[5 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<speed 1>>
It waited through cryosleep.
    -> (answer)
        <<jump SentPingDay2>>
    -> (don't answer)
        I tell myself it's safer to ignore it. Safer to pretend my brain invented the whole thing.
        The ping repeats anyway. Patient. Persistent.
        <<speed 0.4>>
        <<play_sound RobotTest 0.25>>
        "TEST" <i>[79 DAYS AGO]</i>
        <<play_sound RobotHello 0.25>>
        "HELLO" <i>[41 DAYS AGO]</i>
        <<play_sound RobotTalk 0.25>>
        "TALK" <i>[5 DAYS AGO]</i>
        <<speed 1>>
        It's as if it's trying to scare me.
            -> (answer)
                <<jump SentPingDay2>>
===

title: SentPingDay2
position: 259,206
---
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
I press the response key and send a ping back down the line.
As a one-way signal, there's no way to tell what's waiting on the other side. I can only hope the other side taps back.
Either way, my routine is still here.
    -> (try to act normal)
        <<jump RegularTasksDay2>>
===

title: RegularTasksDay2
position: 260,308
---
<<once>>
<<declare $day2DidPushups = false>>
<<declare $day2DidStargaze = false>>
<<declare $day2DidSystemsCheck = false>>
<<endonce>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
I tell myself I can spare a little time before the report.
The ship is silent. My body is still catching up. My thoughts keep circling the ping I sent into the dark.
What to do, what to do...
    -> (do some push-ups) <<if $day2DidPushups == false>>
        <<set $day2DidPushups = true>>
        I drop to the floor and count slowly, careful with my breathing. My arms burn. The burn is familiar, controllable.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        I feel <color=\#88FF88>a little steadier</color> afterwards. It helps, a little.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay2>>
    -> (stare at the stars) <<if $day2DidStargaze == false>>
        <<set $day2DidStargaze = true>>
        I watch the stars until my eyes blur and the ship feels less like a coffin and more like a vehicle.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        For a moment, the vastness doesn't feel threatening. It feels like <color=\#88FF88>something I chose</color>.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay2>>
    -> (check the ship systems) <<if $day2DidSystemsCheck == false>>
        <<set $day2DidSystemsCheck = true>>
        I run quick diagnostics. Life support, comms integrity, power draw. Everything looks normal on paper.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay2>>
    -> (move on to the report)
        <<jump PrepareReportDay2>>
===

title: PrepareReportDay2
